@knowledge tui_design_system
@viewpoints specification
@description {
  The garage49 TUI design system: the themes, color roles, glyphs, surfaces, focus and key rules,
  mouse behaviour, overlays, application frame and the components that every library implements.
}
@scope {
  Define what the design system looks like and how it behaves, independent of any one library, so that
  the Ink and iocraft libraries render the same screen for the same tree. Exclude application logic,
  the libraries' internal structure and the terminal emulators themselves.
}

concept _Theme_ = {
  A named set of semantic color tokens that every component refers to instead of raw colors.
.relations
  changed by _Dim_Theme_
  governed by _Color_Role_
.contract
  - A Theme must provide the tokens text, textMuted, textBright, accent, accentSecondary, heading, success, warning, error, background, panel, surface, surfaceRaised, selectionBackground and selectionText.
  - A component must refer to colors only through a Theme's tokens.
  - The opencode Theme must use the values measured from OpenCode v2.0.21: text #eeeeee, textMuted #808080, textBright #ffffff, accent #fab283, accentSecondary #5c9cf5, heading #9d7cd8, background #0a0a0a, panel #141414, surface #1e1e1e, surfaceRaised #282828, selectionBackground #fab283, selectionText #0a0a0a.
  - The system Theme must use the terminal's ANSI hues for accent, accentSecondary, heading, success, warning and error, and the 256-color gray ramp (232 to 255) for text and background tokens.
  - A library must select the opencode Theme when the terminal reports truecolor and the system Theme otherwise, unless the application names a Theme.
.remarks
  Chosen: success #7fd88f, warning #f5a742 and error #e06c75 come from OpenCode's theme file, not from a measurement; they are provisional.
  Chosen: 16 ANSI colors cannot tell four grays apart, so the system Theme takes its grays from the 256-color ramp; a 16-color terminal still runs with the nearest colors.
}

procedure _Dim_Theme_ = {
  Produce the Theme shown under an open _Overlay_ by pulling every token of a _Theme_ towards black.
.relations
  changes _Theme_
  triggered by _Overlay_
.contract
  - _Dim_Theme_ must scale every truecolor channel and every gray-ramp index by 0.4.
  - _Dim_Theme_ must turn a named ANSI hue into gray and leave black as black.
  - _Dim_Theme_ must apply to the whole screen below the _Overlay_, including the focus bar and any cursor.
}

concept _Color_Role_ = {
  The fixed meaning of each color token, so that a color tells the reader what a thing is.
.relations
  governs _Theme_
  marks _Cursor_
  marks _Focus_Bar_
.contract
  - accent must mark the _Cursor_ and nothing else.
  - accentSecondary must mark the _Focus_Bar_ and the bar of an editing field and nothing else.
  - success, warning and error must mark state values only: a toggle that is on, a chosen radio option, a checked box, a status tone, an error title.
  - heading must mark section headings in lists and the logo block only.
}

concept _Glyph_Set_ = {
  The characters the design system draws states and edges with, kept in one place per library.
.contract
  - Every glyph must be East Asian Width N so it occupies one cell in every terminal; ambiguous-width glyphs such as ● ○ • ■ □ ◉ must not be used.
  - A binary state must use the pair ▪ for on and ▫ for off, in toggles, radio options, filter chips, status dots and the idle spinner.
  - A check box must use ☑ when checked and ☐ otherwise.
  - A tree branch must use ▸ when collapsed and ▾ when expanded.
  - The focus bar, the field bar and the scrollbar thumb must use ┃; the scrollbar track must use │.
  - The active large tab must be marked by ▔ under its label; a surface's bottom edge must use ▀ and a focused input box's foot ╹.
  - Display width must be measured with a width table (string-width or unicode-width), never taken from string length.
}

concept _Surface_ = {
  A screen area told apart from its neighbours by background color alone.
.relations
  shown by _Region_
.contract
  - A _Surface_ must not be separated from its neighbours by line borders.
  - A _Surface_ that ends above other content must end with a half-block edge ▀ in its own color.
  - The sidebar, overlay panels and the status line must use the panel token; inputs, the header label row and dropdowns the surface token; unfocused selections, chips and buttons the surfaceRaised token.
}

concept _Region_ = {
  A focusable screen area that can own the keyboard: the navigation header, the sidebar, the main page, or a field inside a form.
.relations
  blocked by _Overlay_
  shows _Surface_
  shows _Focus_Bar_
  cycled by _Cycle_Focus_
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - A _Region_ must keep its first column free of content.
  - A _Region_ must show the _Focus_Bar_ while it owns the keyboard and nothing in its first column otherwise.
  - A _Region_ must react to keys only while it owns the keyboard and no _Overlay_ is open.
  - A click inside a _Region_ must give it the keyboard.
.remarks
  Chosen: the focus bar is painted over the region's own first column instead of taking a column of its own, so the logo block can start at the screen edge and the bar reads as the region's inner edge.
}

concept _Focus_Bar_ = {
  The blue ┃ column that shows which _Region_ owns the keyboard.
.relations
  hidden by _Overlay_
  shown by _Region_
  marked by _Color_Role_
.contract
  - Exactly one _Focus_Bar_ must be on screen while no _Overlay_ is open.
  - A _Focus_Bar_ must cover the _Region_'s full height unless the _Region_ limits it to its title rows.
  - A _Focus_Bar_ must be painted on the color the _Region_ draws in its first column.
  - A _Focus_Bar_ must use accentSecondary.
}

procedure _Cycle_Focus_ = {
  Move the keyboard from one _Region_ to another by key or by click.
.relations
  cycles _Region_
.contract
  - tab must move to the next _Region_ and shift+tab to the previous one, in screen order from top to bottom and then left to right, wrapping at the ends.
  - enter must move down to the next _Region_ from the navigation header or the sidebar, and esc must move up to the previous one; neither must wrap.
  - Arrow keys and hjkl must not move between Regions; they move inside the focused _Region_.
  - A _Region_ that appears or disappears must enter or leave the cycle at its screen position.
.remarks
  Chosen: a sidebar that is not shown leaves the cycle, so a view without a sidebar cycles between the header and the page only.
}

concept _Cursor_ = {
  The one selected item inside a focused _Region_: a list row, table row, tree row, radio option, chip, button or active tab.
.relations
  belongs to _Region_
  marked by _Color_Role_
.contract
  - A focused _Region_ must show at most one _Cursor_, filled with selectionBackground and drawn in selectionText.
  - A _Region_ that lost the keyboard must keep its _Cursor_ as a surfaceRaised fill.
  - ↑ and ↓ or k and j must move the _Cursor_ one row and stop at the ends.
  - Space or enter must choose or activate the item under the _Cursor_.
  - The wheel must move the _Cursor_ one row per tick where the _Region_ is a list, table or tree.
}

concept _Key_Binding_ = {
  A table entry that names the keys a component reacts to and the action they run.
.relations
  toggles _Theme_
  toggles _Mouse_Reporting_
  guarded by _Typing_State_
.contract
  - A component must declare its keys as a table of bindings, each with its key names and one action, never as a chain of conditions.
  - A key must be named up, down, left, right, pageup, pagedown, home, end, enter, esc, tab, shift+tab, backspace, delete, space, ctrl+x, alt+x, or by its printable character.
  - A printable key that no binding claims must go to the editing text field as text.
  - The application keys must be ctrl+p for the command palette, ? for help, q for the quit confirmation, t to toggle the _Theme_ and m to toggle _Mouse_Reporting_.
}

concept _Typing_State_ = {
  Whether a text field is being edited, so that single-letter application keys stay out of the way.
.relations
  guards _Key_Binding_
.contract
  - While a text field is editing, the keys q, ?, t and m must be inserted as text instead of running application actions.
  - A text field must declare that it is editing while it owns the keyboard and withdraw the declaration when it loses it.
}

concept _Mouse_Reporting_ = {
  The terminal's mouse events delivered to the application and routed to the component under the pointer.
.relations
  focuses _Region_
  limited by _Overlay_
  moves _Cursor_
  toggled by _Key_Binding_
.contract
  - _Mouse_Reporting_ must be on when an application starts and must be turned off when it exits.
  - m must toggle _Mouse_Reporting_, so the terminal's drag-to-select works again while it is off; the status line must show no mouse while it is off.
  - A click must reach every component under the pointer from the innermost to the outermost, so a row click selects the row and gives its _Region_ the keyboard.
  - While an _Overlay_ is open, only components inside the _Overlay_ must react to the mouse.
  - The wheel must move the _Cursor_ in lists, tables and trees and scroll log views and text areas.
}

concept _Overlay_ = {
  One element shown on top of the whole screen through the Screen's single slot: a dialog, the help, the command palette or a dropdown.
.relations
  dims _Theme_
  triggers _Dim_Theme_
  has_member _Confirm_Dialog_
  has_member _Message_Dialog_
  has_member _Help_Overlay_
  has_member _Command_Palette_
  has_member _Dropdown_
.contract
  - At most one _Overlay_ must be open; showing another must replace it.
  - The screen below an open _Overlay_ must be drawn with the dimmed _Theme_.
  - A click outside the _Overlay_ must hide it; esc must hide it.
  - A _Dropdown_ must be anchored under its field; every other _Overlay_ must be centered.
  - An _Overlay_ panel must use the panel token, a bold title at the left and esc muted at the right, and no border.
}

concept _App_Frame_ = {
  The application tree every app is composed as: the frame, an optional navigation header, then content with an optional sidebar and the main page.
.relations
  provides _Theme_
  provides _Mouse_Reporting_
  provides _Cycle_Focus_
  has_part _Navigation_Header_
  has_part _Sidebar_
  has_part _Main_Page_
  has_part _Status_Line_
  has_part _Key_Hint_Bar_
  has_part _Overlay_
.contract
  - An _App_Frame_ must provide the screen, the _Theme_, _Mouse_Reporting_, the _Overlay_ slot, _Cycle_Focus_, the _Status_Line_ and the _Key_Hint_Bar_; an application adds only its regions and pages.
  - An _App_Frame_ must contain a _Navigation_Header_, a _Sidebar_, or both, and always a _Main_Page_.
  - An _App_Frame_ must render the three agreed layouts from the tree alone: a header only, a sidebar only, or both.
  - An _App_Frame_ must show the quit confirmation on q, the help on ?, and the command palette on ctrl+p, and must add Toggle theme, Toggle mouse, Keyboard shortcuts and Quit to the palette.
  - An _App_Frame_ must render at any terminal size and degrade instead of refusing: below 64 columns a layout with a _Sidebar_ keeps the _Sidebar_ alone, below 12 rows the _Key_Hint_Bar_ is dropped, below 8 rows the _Status_Line_ too.
  - An _App_Frame_ may show a notice instead of the layout below a minimum size only when the application sets one; no minimum is set by default.
}

concept _Navigation_Header_ = {
  The two-row header at the top of an _App_Frame_: a logo block, one large tab per view and context text at the right.
.relations
  shows _Focus_Bar_
  is_a _Region_
  has_part _Tabs_
.contract
  - The first row must use the surface token and hold the logo block, the tab labels and the right text; the second row must use the background token and hold the ▔ line under the active tab.
  - The logo block must draw the brand in bold on the heading token and start at the screen edge; its left padding is the _Focus_Bar_'s column, and the bar must cover only the first row.
  - ← and → or h and l must switch the active view while the header owns the keyboard; a click on a tab must switch to it.
}

concept _Sidebar_ = {
  The left panel of an _App_Frame_: a sectioned _List_ of pages, 26 cells wide.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
  hands keyboard to _Main_Page_
  is_a _Region_
  has_part _List_
.contract
  - The _Sidebar_ must use the panel token and keep its _Cursor_ on the current page.
  - ↑ and ↓ or k and j must select the previous or next page; enter must move the keyboard to the _Main_Page_.
}

concept _Main_Page_ = {
  The page area of an _App_Frame_: a bright title, a blank row, then the page; it takes the remaining width.
.relations
  is_a _Region_
.contract
  - The _Main_Page_ must pad two cells on each side and one row above and below, and must clip content that does not fit.
  - enter must not leave the _Main_Page_; it is the page's own key.
}

concept _Status_Line_ = {
  The row above the key hint bar: the last reported action, the application's segments, and at the right the mouse state, theme name, terminal size and clock.
.contract
  - The _Status_Line_ must use the panel token and separate segments with a muted middle dot.
  - The right segments must keep their width; the left segments must be cut to the remaining width with an ellipsis, never run into the right ones.
  - The first segment must be ▪ followed by the last action a page reported, in the success token.
}

concept _Key_Hint_Bar_ = {
  The bottom row: muted context at the left, key and label pairs at the right.
.contract
  - A pair must draw the key in the text token and the label in textMuted, two cells apart from the next pair.
  - A click on a pair must run the key's action; an application's own pair carries its action.
  - The built-in pairs must be tab focus, ctrl+p commands, ? help and q quit, after the application's own.
}

concept _Field_ = {
  A one-row or multi-row form input with a label at the left, a field bar and a value on a surface.
.relations
  is_a _Region_
  has_member _Text_Field_
  has_member _Text_Area_
  has_member _Select_
  has_member _Toggle_
  has_member _Checkbox_
  has_member _Radio_Group_
.contract
  - A _Field_ must draw its label in the text token while editing and textMuted otherwise, with a label width of 14 cells by default.
  - A _Field_ must show a ┃ in accentSecondary on its surface's first column for every row while editing and a blank cell otherwise.
  - A multi-row _Field_ must hand the keyboard to the previous field on ↑ at its first row and to the next field on ↓ at its last row.
  - A click on a _Field_ must make it the editing field.
}

concept _Label_ = {
  Text in one of the theme's roles: default, muted, bright, heading, accent, success, warning or error.
.contract
  - A heading or bright _Label_ must be bold; other roles must be regular weight.
}

concept _List_ = {
  Rows grouped under section headings, with an optional shortcut or value at the right of each row.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - A section heading must be bold in the heading token and be preceded by a blank row except for the first section.
  - A shortcut must be right-aligned in textMuted; a value must be right-aligned in the text token; a row cannot show both.
  - A label that does not fit must be truncated with an ellipsis, never wrapped.
}

concept _Table_ = {
  Rows of fixed-width columns under a muted bold header row.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - A column must have a fixed width and may be right-aligned; columns must be two cells apart.
  - A cell that does not fit must be truncated, never wrapped.
}

concept _Tree_View_ = {
  Hierarchical rows indented two cells per depth with a ▸ or ▾ marker on branches.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - → or l must expand a collapsed branch and otherwise step to the next row; ← or h must collapse an expanded branch and otherwise move to the parent.
  - enter or space must toggle the branch under the _Cursor_.
  - A click on a row must move the _Cursor_ to it; a click on the row's ▸/▾ marker, or on the row the _Cursor_ is already on, must toggle the branch instead (the file-manager convention).
}

concept _Log_View_ = {
  A scrolling list of timestamped, leveled messages with the newest at the bottom and a _Scrollbar_ at the right.
.relations
  has_part _Scrollbar_
.contract
  - A row must draw the time in textMuted in a 9-cell column, the level bold in a 6-cell column (DEBUG textMuted, INFO accentSecondary, WARN warning, ERROR error), then the message; an ERROR message must use the error token.
  - An offset of zero must follow the newest entry; ↑ and ↓ or k and j must scroll one row, pageup and pagedown ten, G or end must return to zero; the wheel must scroll three rows per tick.
}

concept _Scrollbar_ = {
  A one-column indicator at the right of a scrolling view: a faint track with a thumb whose size and position show how much is above and below.
.contract
  - The thumb's length must be the track length times the visible share, at least one cell; its position must be proportional to the offset.
  - The _Scrollbar_ must not be drawn while everything fits.
  - The track must use surfaceRaised and the thumb textMuted.
}

concept _Tabs_ = {
  A row of view labels in two sizes: small inside a page, large in the _Navigation_Header_.
.relations
  used by _Navigation_Header_
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - A small _Tabs_ must be one row and fill the active label as the _Cursor_.
  - A large _Tabs_ must be two rows: the labels, then a ▔ line under the active label; the line must use accent while the tabs own the keyboard and textMuted otherwise.
  - A tab label must be padded two cells on each side; a click on a tab must select it.
}

concept _Text_Field_ = {
  A one-row _Field_ holding a line of text with a █ cursor at the end while editing.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
.contract
  - Typing must append text; backspace must remove the last character; a placeholder in textMuted must show while the value is empty.
  - A secret _Text_Field_ must show one * per character instead of the value.
  - Keys that arrive faster than the screen is redrawn must each apply to the latest value, never to the value of the last drawn frame.
}

concept _Text_Area_ = {
  A multi-row _Field_ holding lines of text with the cursor drawn as the inverted cell, and a _Scrollbar_.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
  has_part _Scrollbar_
.contract
  - Arrow keys must move the cursor by character and by line; enter must split the line at the cursor; backspace must remove the character before the cursor or join the line with the previous one at column zero.
  - pageup and pagedown must move the cursor by the visible row count; home and end must move it within the line.
  - The wheel must scroll the view three rows without moving the cursor; moving the cursor must bring it back into view.
  - Text must be handled by character, so a CJK character or an emoji is one cursor step.
}

concept _Input_Box_ = {
  OpenCode's command input: a bar column, three rows of surface with the text on the middle row, an optional footer row and a half-block bottom edge.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
.contract
  - While editing, the bar column must show ┃ in accentSecondary on every row and the bottom edge must start with ╹; otherwise the bar column is blank and the edge is all ▀.
  - enter must submit the value; typing and backspace edit it.
}

concept _Select_ = {
  A one-row _Field_ showing the chosen option and ▾, which opens a _Dropdown_ of options.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
  opens _Dropdown_
.contract
  - enter, space or a click must open the _Dropdown_ anchored under the value; ← and → must cycle the option without opening it.
}

concept _Toggle_ = {
  A one-row _Field_ for a boolean, drawn as ▪ on in the success token or ▫ off in textMuted on a surface.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
.contract
  - space, enter or a click must flip the value.
}

concept _Checkbox_ = {
  A one-row _Field_ on the background drawn as ☑ in the success token or ☐ in textMuted before its label.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
.contract
  - space, enter or a click must flip the value.
}

concept _Radio_Group_ = {
  A multi-row _Field_ with one option per row: ▪ in the success token for the chosen option, ▫ in textMuted for the others, and a _Cursor_ row.
.relations
  is_a _Field_
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - ↑ and ↓ or k and j must move the _Cursor_ without choosing; space or enter must choose the option under the _Cursor_; a click must choose directly.
  - The _Cursor_ must start on the chosen option when the field takes the keyboard.
}

concept _Button_ = {
  A label on a raised surface, padded two cells, that runs an action.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - The chosen _Button_ of a dialog must be the _Cursor_; the others must use surfaceRaised.
  - A click must run the action.
}

concept _Chip_ = {
  A small pill on a raised surface: a tag, a filter or a status.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
.contract
  - A tag _Chip_ must show × at its right and remove itself when × is clicked or when x or backspace is pressed under the _Cursor_.
  - A filter _Chip_ must show ▪ when on and ▫ when off and flip on click.
  - A status _Chip_ must color its label with the status tone; the pill itself stays on surfaceRaised so tone reads as a value, not a _Cursor_.
}

concept _Spinner_ = {
  An in-progress marker in accentSecondary with an optional muted label.
.contract
  - A _Spinner_ must advance one frame every 160 milliseconds in one of the frame sets dots, line or bounce.
  - An inactive _Spinner_ must show ▪ instead of animating.
}

concept _Confirm_Dialog_ = {
  A centered _Overlay_ with a title, a message and two buttons, cancel and confirm.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
  is_a _Overlay_
  has_part _Button_
.contract
  - The confirm _Button_ must be the _Cursor_ only after ← → or tab moves there; cancel is chosen first.
  - enter must run the chosen button; y must confirm, n and esc must cancel.
  - A destructive _Confirm_Dialog_ must draw its title in the error token.
}

concept _Message_Dialog_ = {
  A centered _Overlay_ with a title, a message and one OK button.
.relations
  is_a _Overlay_
  has_part _Button_
.contract
  - enter, esc or a click on OK must close it; an error _Message_Dialog_ must draw its title in the error token.
}

concept _Help_Overlay_ = {
  A centered _Overlay_ listing key bindings, one row per entry with the keys in the text token and the action in textMuted.
.relations
  lists _App_Frame_
  is_a _Overlay_
.contract
  - The _Help_Overlay_ must list the _App_Frame_'s keys first and the application's entries after them.
  - esc, ? or q must close it.
}

concept _Command_Palette_ = {
  A centered _Overlay_ with a search line and a sectioned _List_ of commands filtered by the query.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
  is_a _Overlay_
  has_part _List_
.contract
  - Typing must filter the commands by label, case-insensitively; backspace must shorten the query.
  - ↑ and ↓ must move the _Cursor_; enter or a click must run the command and close the palette.
}

concept _Dropdown_ = {
  An _Overlay_ anchored under a _Select_: a _List_ of options on a surface, without blank rows above or below.
.relations
  has_member _Cursor_
  is_a _Overlay_
  has_part _List_
  opened by _Select_
.contract
  - The _Cursor_ must start on the chosen option; ↑ and ↓ move it; enter or a click picks and closes.
}

concept _Library_ = {
  An implementation of the design system for one UI library: @garage49/garage49-tui-ink for Ink on Node.js and garage49-tui-iocraft for iocraft on Rust.
.relations
  restores _Mouse_Reporting_
  implements _App_Frame_
  shown by _Gallery_
.contract
  - A _Library_ must render the same screen as every other _Library_ for the same tree, checked in a 110 by 32 cell terminal.
  - A _Library_ must restore the terminal on exit, on panic and on ctrl+c: raw mode, the alternate screen, the cursor and _Mouse_Reporting_.
  - A _Library_ must handle resize at any size and must draw CJK and emoji at their display width without broken wrapping or truncation.
  - A _Library_ must work under SSH, tmux and Herdr.
.remarks
  Chosen: the Ink and iocraft libraries were chosen over OpenTUI and ratatui because both are component models with hooks and flexbox layout, so one design system maps onto both.
  Chosen: in iocraft a component that listens to the mouse has a View as its root element, because local mouse events do not reach a component whose root is another component.
}

concept _Gallery_ = {
  A sample application per _Library_ that shows every element of the design system, one page each, built on the _App_Frame_.
.relations
  built on _App_Frame_
  shows _Library_
.contract
  - A _Gallery_ must show every component of this Knowledge and the four views Gallery, Dashboard, Settings and Help.
  - The galleries of all libraries must render the same screen for the same page, compared before a change to the design system is accepted.
}
